<rml>
<head>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="theme.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="newchar_common.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="newchartraits.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="newchartraits">
    <!-- Tier 4 screen #4 (new-character creator): the TRAITS tab (set_traits).
         ROW based, after UI_designs/11_charcreation_mutations.png: three columns of
         single-line rows separated by dotted rules, each row a set of aligned
         micro-columns — cursor, checkbox, cost tag, name — so a 60-row column can be
         scanned down any one of them. Cards were tried first and were not readable at
         this item count; see plans/charcreation-traits-tree.md.

         Column 3 carries sub-headings (Neutral, then one per appearance mutation type,
         derived from mandatory_one / swap_on_conflict). A heading occupies a row of the
         SAME height as an item, which is what keeps the cursor-scroll arithmetic exact.

         Keyboard: LEFT/RIGHT change column, UP/DOWN move within it, CONFIRM takes or
         drops, RANDOMIZE, REROLL_*, NEXT/PREV_TAB, QUIT. Mouse: row selects, the
         checkbox toggles. -->
    <div class="panel nc-panel">
        <div class="nc-steps">
            <div class="nc-step" data-for="t : tabs"
                 data-class-selected="t.selected" data-class-done="t.done">
                <div class="nc-step-icon" data-style-decorator="t.icon_dec"></div>
                <span class="nc-step-label" data-rml="t.name_rml"></span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="nc-shell">
            <!-- Navigators. Shortcut text comes from the real binding via
                 input_context::get_desc, so it stays correct after a rebind. -->
            <div class="nc-arrow nc-arrow-prev" data-if="has_prev"
                 data-event-click="on_prev()">
                <div class="nc-arrow-glyph">&#60;</div>
                <div class="nc-arrow-key" data-rml="prev_key_rml"></div>
                <div class="nc-arrow-dest" data-rml="prev_name_rml"></div>
            </div>
            <div class="nc-arrow-spacer" data-if="!has_prev"></div>
            <div class="nc-stage">
                <!-- Meta bar: pools on the left, the trait budget on the right, dotted
                     rules above and below it as in the reference. -->
                <div class="nc-rule"></div>
                <div class="nc-trait-top">
                    <span class="nc-trait-points" data-rml="points_rml"></span>
                    <span class="nc-trait-budget" data-rml="budget_rml"></span>
                </div>
                <div class="nc-rule"></div>
                <!-- Own row, not inside .nc-trait-top: at 230dp wedged between the points
                     and cost lines the scale read as clutter rather than as an indicator.
                     It is the one screen-level readout of both budgets. -->
                <div class="nc-balance-row" data-if="balance.show">
                    <!-- No absolute positioning anywhere: RmlUi resolved `position: absolute`
                         against .nc-panel rather than against .nc-scale's `position: relative`,
                         which put the beam ~39dp above the pans and across the top bar. Pure
                         flow instead: arm row (pan | beam | pan) with the fulcrum beneath. -->
                    <div class="nc-scale">
                        <div class="nc-scale-arm">
                            <div class="nc-scale-pan" data-style-top="balance.good_top">
                                <div class="nc-scale-icon" data-style-decorator="balance.good_icon"></div>
                                <span class="nc-scale-num" data-rml="balance.good_rml"></span>
                            </div>
                            <div class="nc-scale-beam" data-style-transform="balance.rotate"></div>
                            <div class="nc-scale-pan" data-style-top="balance.bad_top">
                                <span class="nc-scale-num" data-rml="balance.bad_rml"></span>
                                <div class="nc-scale-icon" data-style-decorator="balance.bad_icon"></div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="nc-scale-fulcrum" data-style-decorator="balance.fulcrum_icon"></div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="nc-trait-cols">
                    <!-- Three columns, written out rather than generated, because each needs a
                         stable id for C++ to scroll its own cursor into view. -->
                    <div class="nc-trait-colwrap">
                        <div class="nc-trait-colhead">
                            <span class="nc-trait-colname" data-rml="col0.name_rml"></span>
                            <span class="nc-trait-colcount" data-rml="col0.count_rml"></span>
                        </div>
                        <div id="nc-trait-col0" class="nc-trait-list">
                            <div class="item nc-trait-row" data-for="r, ri : col0.rows"
                                 data-class-selected="r.selected" data-class-header="r.header"
                                 data-event-click="on_row(0, ri)">
                                <span class="nc-tr-cursor" data-rml="r.cursor_rml"></span>
                                <span class="nc-tr-check" data-rml="r.check_rml"
                                      data-event-click="on_check(0, ri)"></span>
                                <span class="nc-tr-cost" data-rml="r.cost_rml"></span>
                                <span class="nc-tr-name" data-rml="r.name_rml"></span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="nc-vrule"></div>
                    <div class="nc-trait-colwrap">
                        <div class="nc-trait-colhead">
                            <span class="nc-trait-colname" data-rml="col1.name_rml"></span>
                            <span class="nc-trait-colcount" data-rml="col1.count_rml"></span>
                        </div>
                        <div id="nc-trait-col1" class="nc-trait-list">
                            <div class="item nc-trait-row" data-for="r, ri : col1.rows"
                                 data-class-selected="r.selected" data-class-header="r.header"
                                 data-event-click="on_row(1, ri)">
                                <span class="nc-tr-cursor" data-rml="r.cursor_rml"></span>
                                <span class="nc-tr-check" data-rml="r.check_rml"
                                      data-event-click="on_check(1, ri)"></span>
                                <span class="nc-tr-cost" data-rml="r.cost_rml"></span>
                                <span class="nc-tr-name" data-rml="r.name_rml"></span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="nc-vrule"></div>
                    <div class="nc-trait-colwrap">
                        <div class="nc-trait-colhead">
                            <span class="nc-trait-colname" data-rml="col2.name_rml"></span>
                            <span class="nc-trait-colcount" data-rml="col2.count_rml"></span>
                        </div>
                        <div id="nc-trait-col2" class="nc-trait-list">
                            <div class="item nc-trait-row" data-for="r, ri : col2.rows"
                                 data-class-selected="r.selected" data-class-header="r.header"
                                 data-event-click="on_row(2, ri)">
                                <span class="nc-tr-cursor" data-rml="r.cursor_rml"></span>
                                <span class="nc-tr-check" data-rml="r.check_rml"
                                      data-event-click="on_check(2, ri)"></span>
                                <span class="nc-tr-cost" data-rml="r.cost_rml"></span>
                                <span class="nc-tr-name" data-rml="r.name_rml"></span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="nc-rule"></div>
                <!-- ":: TRAIT NAME" over the detail panel, as in the reference. -->
                <div class="nc-trait-selname" data-rml="sel_name_rml"></div>
                <div class="nc-info-panel">
                    <!-- Art slot: the character portrait, which already wears the selected kit.
                         It earns its place on this tab more than any other — taking a visible
                         mutation changes it. -->
                    <div class="nc-info-art" data-if="has_portrait"
                         data-style-decorator="portrait_dec"></div>
                    <div class="nc-info-facts">
                        <div class="nc-fact" data-for="f : facts">
                            <div class="nc-fact-label" data-rml="f.label_rml"></div>
                            <div class="nc-fact-value" data-rml="f.value_rml"></div>
                            <!-- Carries the reason an unavailable trait cannot be taken, which
                                 used to exist only as a popup AFTER pressing CONFIRM. -->
                            <div class="nc-fact-sub" data-rml="f.sub_rml"></div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <!-- Prose in a .nc-info-blurb CHILD: .nc-info-desc is `display: flex`, and a
                         bare text node in a flex container gets no inline context and renders
                         nothing. See plans/charcreation-stats-cards.md. -->
                    <div class="nc-info-desc">
                        <div class="nc-info-blurb" data-rml="desc_rml"></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="nc-trait-hint" data-rml="hint_rml"></div>
            </div>
            <div class="nc-arrow nc-arrow-next" data-if="has_next"
                 data-event-click="on_next()">
                <div class="nc-arrow-glyph">&#62;</div>
                <div class="nc-arrow-key" data-rml="next_key_rml"></div>
                <div class="nc-arrow-dest" data-rml="next_name_rml"></div>
            </div>
            <div class="nc-arrow-spacer" data-if="!has_next"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="nc-exit" data-rml="exit_rml"></div>
    </div>
    <div id="crt-overlay" class="crt"></div>
</body>
</rml>
